, "Strix varia", "Didelphis virginiana"], "opossum>coyote": ["g", "Canis latrans", "Didelphis virginiana"], "otter>coyote": ["g", "Canis latrans", "Lontra canadensis"], "watersnake>owl": ["gg", "Strix varia", "Nerodia erythrogaster"], "deer>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Odocoileus virginianus"], "boar>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Sus scrofa"], "beaver>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Castor canadensis"], "raccoon>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Procyon lotor"], "opossum>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Didelphis virginiana"], "coyote>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Canis latrans"], "squirrel>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Sciurus niger"], "deer>raccoon": ["ga", "Procyon lotor", "Odocoileus virginianus"], "boar>raccoon": ["ga", "Procyon lotor", "Sus scrofa"], "deer>opossum": ["ga", "Didelphis virginiana", "Odocoileus virginianus"], "deer>owl": ["ga", "Strix varia", "Odocoileus virginianus"]}, "story": "Congaree National Park in central South Carolina preserves the largest tract of old-growth bottomland hardwood forest left in the United States. Its floodplain trees are some of the tallest in the eastern US, forming one of the highest temperate deciduous forest canopies remaining in the world.", "matters": "It is often called a swamp, but it is mostly bottomland that floodwaters cover from time to time. A grassroots campaign that began in 1969 led to its protection."}